# .mailmap — canonical identity mapping for local git tooling.
#
# This file makes `git log %aN`, `git shortlog` and `git blame` in this repo
# report one identity for the owner, instead of splitting across the two
# addresses the owner has authored commits with.
#
# It does NOT affect the GitHub contributors sidebar. GitHub builds that list
# from commit authors and from `Co-authored-by` co-authors, and it does not
# consult `.mailmap` when it does so — verified against the live repository on
# 2026-10-20, where a mailmap covering both the Dependabot App address and
# the co-author address left the sidebar unchanged. The sidebar was fixed by
# rewriting the history instead (trailers stripped, bot-authored commits
# re-attributed), which is the only mechanism GitHub honours.
#
# Format:  Proper Name <proper@email>  <commit name> <commit@email>
#
# The `proper@email` is the account's own GitHub noreply, which is the
# canonical address GitHub links to the `yuno7777` account.

# The repository owner authored commits under two addresses, both linked to
# the same GitHub account. Pin the canonical one so they cannot split.
Abhishek Satarkar <69352090+yuno7777@users.noreply.github.com> <abhisheksatarkar098@gmail.com>
